     src=[('Geography textbook (paraphrased)', 'Settlements can be arranged in a hierarchy. At the bottom are many small hamlets and villages offering few, low-order services. Towards the top are fewer but larger towns and cities offering many services, including high-order ones such as universities, specialist hospitals and international airports.', 'Paraphrase of a standard explanation of the settlement hierarchy in secondary-school geography textbooks, based on Christaller\'s central place theory (1933)', 'to explain a model to students', 'It summarises a widely used model clearly.', 'Models simplify reality; online shopping and car travel have changed how people use services.', 'There are many small settlements with few services and few large ones with many services.')],
