     evaluate=[('Individuals are mainly responsible for making lifestyles more sustainable.', ['consumer choices about food, travel and waste shape demand', 'collective individual action can change markets'], ['about 70% of industrial emissions since 1988 have been linked to around 100 fossil-fuel producers (CDP 2017)', 'governments set the rules and infrastructure that make sustainable choices possible'], 'Individuals have a role, but governments and businesses carry the greater responsibility because they shape the systems within which individuals choose.')],
     src=[('Report extract (paraphrased)', 'The commission defined sustainable development as development that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs. It stressed that the needs of the world\'s poor should be given overriding priority.', 'Paraphrase of the World Commission on Environment and Development, "Our Common Future" (the Brundtland Report), 1987', 'to set out a global vision linking environment and development for governments', 'It is the source of the most widely used definition of sustainable development.', 'It is a statement of principles agreed by a commission and gives no measurable targets or ways to enforce them.', 'Development must meet present needs, especially of the poor, without harming future generations.')],
